# The metrics face of one pipeline, as the HTTP control plane renders it: GET /api/pipelines/{id}/metrics.
#
# Every reader of this face is outside this build -- a dashboard, a script, the command line of a
# release already shipped -- and none of them is told when a field moves. This file is what tells the
# build. A line here changing means one of them has to be told, in the release note, which field it was.
#
# The fixture is fixed and renders one of everything the face carries: the flat map with a squeezed
# family and a bare key, an acked position, the names of the positions not collected, and the facts --
# a counter broken down by attributes with one overflow series, a gauge with no attributes, a gauge per
# table, a counter per code, and a distribution over the registered bounds.
#
# Rendered with two-space indentation so it reads as lines; the server sends the same bytes without the
# whitespace. Blank lines and lines starting with # are prose and are not compared.

